      "message": "nit: rather than matching on len() and then still needing the (potentially fallible, though not really in practice) `try_into()` to get the value out of an Option, you could use the `try_into()` itself to check whether the size matches, something like:\n\n```\nif let Some(val) \u003d bytes.try_into().ok().map(u32::from_be_bytes) {\n    Some(DeviceTreeInteger::SingleCell(val))\n} else if let Some(val) \u003d bytes.try_into().ok().map(u64::from_be_bytes) {\n    Some(DeviceTreeInteger::DoubleCell(val))\n} else {\n    None\n}\n```",
